DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: what a differential does.
# Model: Flywheel differential (motor A turns the differential's 28-tooth gear through a
# 12-tooth bevel gear; motor C can hold the right wheel through two bevel gears).
# The gears inside share the turn between the two wheels.
# Right wheel held: the left wheel turns twice as fast as the differential.
# Right wheel turned as fast as the differential: the left wheel turns that fast too.
# (Motor C at 36 turns the right wheel as fast as motor A at 50 turns the differential:
# 12 teeth to 28 for motor A, 12 to 20 for motor C.)
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action C hold
  stop motor C
  set motor speed A 30
  start motor A forward
  wait 5 seconds
  set motor speed C 22
  start motor C forward
  wait 5 seconds
  stop motor A
  stop motor C
